This is round 2 of scripts/agent/launch.sh (a launcher that starts a job in a transient systemd --user unit and a watcher that waits for it). Round 1 findings it must fix: systemd-run expanded ${VAR}/%specifiers in the command; --dir overwrote an existing job dir; a TOCTOU race between the status-file check and is-active; --collect unloaded the unit before its Result was read; the WAIT line was not shell-quoted; a missing user bus must be an operational error (2), not a lost unit (125). Check that each is truly fixed, that the controls in scripts/checks/agent_launch.sh would fail without the fix, and look for new defects (e.g. unit left loaded forever, leaked failed units, wrong exit codes, a successful unit garbage-collected before status is seen).
This is the whole launcher branch (three commits: initial, round-2 and round-3 fixes, the latter fixing: run_job exits 0 iff status written else 2; cached result readback; ''/success -> unknown; --dir trailing slash). Also check AGENTS.md subsection, RETENTION.tsv row, root_inventory entry, and the changelog fragment.
